    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475-a1">

                <pb facs="0488" n="1222" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1222"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 350.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr.
                            Uhl.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Havana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1895-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7,
                                1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2439.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon information received in a letter dated
                    the 27th ultimo, from our vice-commercial agent at Caibarien, Mr. James H.
                    Springer, <pb facs="0489" n="1223" xml:id="pg1223"/> to the effect that Mr.
                    Francisco Carrillo, a citizen of the United States, had been arrested at the
                    neighboring town of San Juan de los Remedios, I have addressed a communication
                    to His Excellency the Governor-General, asking that this American citizen be
                    tried by the civil and not by the military jurisdiction, according to and with
                    the enjoyment of all the guarantees of the agreement of the 12th of January,
                    1877, between Spain and the United States.</p>
                <p>For the information of the Department, I enclose translation of my communication
                    to the Governor-General.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
